NAME
     stat - what the inode says about a file

SYNOPSIS
     stat [-L] [-t] [-c FORMAT] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     stat prints the inode: type, size in bytes and blocks, mode, owner
     and group, link count, device and inode number, and the three
     times. A symbolic link is reported as itself unless -L is given.
     Called as readlink, it prints what a symbolic link points at
     instead.

OPTIONS
     -L   follow symbolic links
     -t   one line, in the order the fields appear in struct stat
     -c FORMAT
          print FORMAT with %n the name, %s the size, %b blocks, %f raw
          mode, %a mode in octal, %u %U owner, %g %G group, %i inode,
          %h links, %F the kind of thing it is

SEE ALSO
     ls(1), file(1), readlink(1)
